        <mxCell id="n_route" value="&lt;div style=&#x27;font-family:Helvetica;font-size:13px;font-weight:bold;color:#12212E&#x27;&gt;Routing gotcha  —  open gap&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&#x27;height:8px&#x27;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&#x27;font-family:Consolas,monospace;font-size:11px;color:#22333F;line-height:15px&#x27;&gt;GENERATOR_MODEL and EVALUATOR_MODEL are single GLOBAL&lt;br&gt;settings, not per-section. Pointing GENERATOR_MODEL at a&lt;br&gt;reading-only fine-tune would hijack every listening call&lt;br&gt;too. That is precisely why the retrain is ONE multi-task&lt;br&gt;LoRA over the combined 439-record corpus.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;A configured fine-tune always routes to a local Ollama&lt;br&gt;client regardless of LLM_PROVIDER; a blank setting falls&lt;br&gt;back to the general hosted model.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;One global asyncio semaphore serialises ALL ollama calls,&lt;br&gt;so a 5-minute generator call blocks evaluator marking.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;arcSize=6;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=12;spacingTop=8;spacingRight=10;fillColor=#FBF0F3;strokeColor=#B00020;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1330" y="896" width="400" height="236" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
